OpenMail
========

A mail reader for OPENSTEP 4.2 in the style of NeXTMail, talking to current
IMAP servers over TLS.  It is built on Pantomime (the `pantomime` package) and
written in Objective-C with the OPENSTEP AppKit; there is no nib file, the
windows are made in code.

This is version 0.1, the foundation: it connects, lists the mailboxes and
shows a mailbox's messages with the text of the selected one.  It cannot yet
compose or send, flag, delete or move messages, show attachments or HTML, or
keep a local copy.  Those are the next steps, in about that order.  OAuth 2
(Gmail, Microsoft 365) is planned for a later major version; for now the
server must accept a password.

Running it
----------

    /usr/local/Apps/OpenMail.app/OpenMail

or open the application in the Workspace Manager (it is in `/usr/local/Apps`;
link it into `/LocalApps` or add it to the dock if you like).  The first time,
the account panel asks for the servers.  Everything except the password is kept
in your defaults (`defaults read OpenMail`); the password is asked for at each
start and is not stored.

  * Incoming mail (IMAP): the server, a security setting and the port.
    "Encrypted (TLS)" on 993 is the usual one; "Start TLS" is for 143.
  * Outgoing mail (SMTP): saved now, used when sending is added.
  * "Check the server's certificate" is on by default.  The certificates are
    checked against /usr/local/ssl/cert.pem (the `ca-certificates` package);
    give a file in "Certificates file" to trust your own authority instead.
    Turn the check off only on a network you control.

The Mailboxes window lists the server's mailboxes; double-click one to open it.
Selecting a message shows its headers and text in the lower half.  Mailbox ->
Check Mail asks the server again.

The windows wait for the network (names are looked up, and the TLS handshake
is done, without returning to the event loop), so the interface can pause for
a moment while connecting.

Testing without a display
-------------------------

`openmail-sessiontest` runs the same session code with no windows:

    PMAIL_PASSWORD=... openmail-sessiontest host 993 tls user [cafile|-k] [mailbox]

It lists the mailboxes, opens one, prints the senders and subjects and the text
of the last message.  `pkg test openmail` runs it against a closed port to check
that failures are reported, and, if `OPENMAIL_TEST_SERVER` (host[:port]),
`OPENMAIL_TEST_USER` and `PMAIL_PASSWORD` are set (and `OPENMAIL_TEST_CAFILE`,
if needed), against a real server.

Layout of the source
--------------------

  Account.[hm]        the settings, in the defaults
  MailSession.[hm]    one IMAP conversation (Foundation only; tested on Linux
                      against Dovecot with Pantomime's linux-test servers)
  Windows.[hm]        the Mailboxes and Viewer windows
  AccountPanel.[hm]   the account panel and the password prompt
  MailApp.[hm]        the application delegate and the menus
  UIKit.[hm]          helpers that build controls in code
